  "objective": "Start the first pass in the manual's order (boom to height, solution pump, rate, move off, AutoTrac, sections, master), index sections off for a waterway, change rate on the move, run a headland with HMS in the right order and resume AutoTrac, then do the next headland by hand with HMS off.",
  "procedure_source": "612R operator's manual OMKK105338: Field Operation (p. 50-21 to 50-23), Operate Indexed Boom Sections (p. 50-23, 50-24), Operate Boom Return to Height (p. 50-24, 50-25), Multi-Function Lever (p. 30-17 to 30-19), Headland Management System application (p. 25-D-1 to 25-D-7), Target Rate/Rx (p. 25-I-5), Operate AutoTrac (p. 140-3, 140-4). Steps marked draft are adapted for the simulator (single HMS button, AutoTrac Resume mapped to switch 4, the scenario's rate and speed changes): confirm with an operator.",
  "setup": {
    "armrest": [
      "switch foot_switch 0",
      "switch park_slot 1",
      "set steering 0",
      "set speed_dial 0",
      "switch foot_switch 1",
      "wait 0.3",
      "press centre_boom_lower 800",
      "wait 0.3",
      "switch foot_switch 0",
      "wait 0.3",
      "press centre_boom_raise 600",
      "press engine_high_idle 300",
      "set speed_dial 8",
      "switch park_slot 0",
      "set lever 125",
      "wait 0.5"
    ],
    "trainer": "612R at the start of the first pass. Boom unfolded with the centre frame raised, engine at high idle, lever out of the park slot in neutral, park brake released, speed wheel 8 clicks up, wheel straight, solution pump OFF, master OFF. Display: Target Rate/Rx presets set from the product label (Rate 1 = this field's rate, Rate 3 = heavy-patch rate), guidance line set and Steer On, Return to Height set. HMS ON and Ready: Entering Headlands = Master Spray OFF and Boom Return to Height - Raise; Exiting Headlands = Boom Return to Height - Lower (Master Spray ON and AutoTrac Resume not ticked). Before section 4, turn HMS OFF on the display.",
    "expect": {
      "game": {
        "boomUnfolded": "1"
      }
    }
  },
  "chatbot": {
    "about": "The trainee is starting to spray with a John Deere 612R (CommandCenter display, CommandARM) on the simulator. The lesson follows the 612R operator's manual OMKK105338: the Field Operation order (boom to operating height, solution pump, rate switch 1/2/3, lever slowly forward, sections enabled, master), IBS buttons (IBS Right shuts sections off starting at the left-hand end, IBS Left starting at the right-hand end, IBS Reset restarts all shut-off sections), HMS (here: entering = Master Spray OFF + Boom Return to Height - Raise; exiting = Boom Return to Height - Lower) and AutoTrac Resume (AutoTrac switches off when the wheel is turned more than 30°; the operator steers at the end of the track). Application rates come from the product label and the display presets, not the manual. Answer in 2-3 sentences, only from the manual, and name the exact control.",
